Q: Plotly, have one dropdown menu for each level in DataFrame multi-index A: <p>You could create a button for each date, with all possible categories available in the dropdown. I have also added an &quot;All&quot; button to toggle all traces, in case this is something you would like.</p>
<p>`updatemenus = [dict(x=0.5, y=1.2, xanchor=&quot;center&quot;, showactive=True, buttons=[
dict(label=&quot;All&quot;, method=&quot;restyle&quot;, visible=True, args=[{&quot;visible&quot;: [True for col in columns]}])
])]
num_buttons = len(dates)
for i,date in enumerate(dates):
print(f&quot;processing date = {date}, i = {i}&quot;)
date_columns = [col for col in columns if col[0] == date]
date_short = date.strftime(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)
updatemenus.append(dict(
x=1.00*i/num_buttons, y=1.00, xanchor=&quot;center&quot;, showactive=True,
buttons=[
dict(label=f&quot;{date_short} {c}&quot;, method=&quot;restyle&quot;, visible=True, args=[{
&quot;visible&quot;: [(col[0] == d and col[1] == c) for col in columns],
}])
for (d,c) in date_columns
],
),)</p>
<p>fig.update_layout(updatemenus=updatemenus)`</p>
